    {
      "id": "7356dafd-2e6a-4609-8d93-386b8dc1ddd4",
      "name": "📌 Overview – How This Workflow Works1",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -3920,
        2432
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 2,
        "width": 780,
        "height": 672,
        "content": "## 📅 Meeting Prep Automation – AI Agenda Generator\n\n### How it works\nEvery morning, the workflow reads upcoming Google Calendar events and cross-references them against a Google Sheets log to skip already-processed meetings. For each new meeting, attendee domain data is enriched via the Hunter API, and the meeting is classified as Internal or External before the AI call. Gmail is searched for recent related emails to build context. GPT-4o-mini generates a structured agenda — purpose, prep tasks, talking points, outcomes. High-priority agendas (with substantial content) trigger a Slack notification to the team channel before the draft is sent. All runs are audited to Airtable. A Telegram alert and Sheets log confirm each prep cycle.\n\n### Setup steps\n1. Connect **Google Calendar OAuth2** and set your calendar ID.\n2. Connect **Gmail OAuth2** to `Search Related Emails` and `Create Gmail Draft`.\n3. Connect **OpenAI API** to `AI Generate Agenda`.\n4. Connect **Google Sheets OAuth2** → replace `REPLACE_WITH_YOUR_MEETING_PREP_SHEET_ID`.\n5. Connect **Telegram Bot API** → replace `REPLACE_WITH_YOUR_TELEGRAM_CHAT_ID`.\n6. Connect **Slack OAuth2** → replace `YOUR_SLACK_CHANNEL_ID` in both Slack nodes.\n7. Add your **Hunter API key** in `Enrich Attendee Data`.\n8. Connect **Airtable PAT** → replace base ID and table ID.\n9. Activate the schedule trigger."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "4c0bcd23-af7d-42d2-b52e-296013464019",
      "name": "Section – Calendar Fetch & Deduplication1",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -3072,
        2448
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 796,
        "height": 952,
        "content": "## 📆 Calendar Fetch & Deduplication\nFires daily. Reads upcoming events from Google Calendar and fetches already-processed event IDs from Google Sheets in parallel. A code node filters out events already in the log — so meetings are only prepped once across multiple runs."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "57ffb818-5952-419c-b6c8-f8a273aab057",
      "name": "🔑 Credentials & Configuration1",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        1680,
        3056
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 3,
        "width": 368,
        "height": 332,
        "content": "## 🔑 Credentials Required\n- **Google Calendar OAuth2** — event fetch\n- **Gmail OAuth2** — email search + draft\n- **OpenAI API** — agenda generation\n- **Google Sheets OAuth2** — dedup + log\n- **Telegram Bot API** — alert + error\n- **Slack OAuth2** — team channel + error\n- **Hunter API** — attendee enrichment\n- **Airtable PAT** — audit log"
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "bace983b-742c-4c60-9033-8dceb468745b",
      "name": "Section – P2 Email Context & Enrichment",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
